window.EN={"1":"Having broken through the castle gate, Leif's \"Liberation Army\" pours into the castle all at once.","2":"Their one and only goal: the throne of Leonster Castle.","3":"The restoration of the kingdom, the long-cherished wish of Leif and his people, was becoming a reality...","4":"Xavier! You understand, don't you!!","5":"Understand what...?","6":"I did not kill you, a defeated general, and for these ten-odd years I have favored you as my right hand.","7":"You have not forgotten that debt, I trust!","8":"Debt? ...I, too, believe I have worked hard for you, Marquis...","9":"Mm, you have certainly been useful. But I believe I have granted your requests as far as I could, too.","10":"Heh...","11":"What? Are you saying you have a complaint! If you do, say it.","12":"It is already too late. The dead do not come back to life...","13":"Ugh... In any case, Xavier, you and I are equally guilty.","14":"They resent you as a traitor.","15":"Even if you tried to switch sides now, they would not accept you.","16":"I am well aware of that! How could I show my face and meet them now?","17":"Marquis, you need not be afraid. As a warrior of sorts, I at least know how to meet my end!!","18":"August, was this really the right thing? Isn't dividing our forces dangerous?","19":"To keep the treasures in the castle from being carried off, it is better to split into two groups. Besides, rescuing the hostages is necessary too.","20":"And persuading General Xavier?","21":"I must say it is quite difficult.","22":"We free the hostages and have them persuade the eight heavy knights under the general's command,","23":"but if the imperial soldiers on watch spot them, everything is over. Do not let your guard down...","24":"Understood. Then, everyone, let's go!","25":"Let us raise this banner of Gae Bolg once more over the royal castle of Leonster!","26":"Father! Stop it now!","27":"Ohh, you were safe! Thank goodness... With you back, who'd work for the Empire!","28":"Dear!","29":"So you were safe! Then there's no need to be here any longer. Come, let's go home...","30":"Dad! It's me! Dad!","31":"What! How did you get here? ...Well, never mind that. Anyway, let's get out of here quick!","32":"Stop it now! You don't have to fight anymore!","33":"...As long as you're safe, I have no business here. Let's get away together!","34":"Hey! What are you doing in a place like this! We're getting out of here, now!","35":"No, well, you were captured so I had no choice... Hey, wait for me~","36":"I'm sorry... All this, because of me...","37":"It's fine, it's fine. As long as you're safe, Pops, that's all that matters. Come on, let's go...","38":"......","39":"It's all right, Mother. You don't have to say anything. Come, let's go home...","40":"Waaah, Daddy...","41":"There, there, it's all right now. Come on, let's go home together with Daddy, okay?","42":"General Xavier!?","43":"Prince Leif... You have grown up splendidly... I had wished to see you just once.","44":"With this, I have nothing left to regret.","45":"General, what are you saying? I...","46":"No.","47":"Whatever the reason may have been, it does not change the fact that I betrayed the lord to whom I owed so much.","48":"But Prince, the guilt lies with this old man alone.","49":"Please, forgive my subordinates. Everything was at my order. My subordinates bear no guilt.","50":"General... What a man you are...","51":"Please, raise your head. I am the one who must apologize.","52":"I should have protected the people, yet I abandoned them and fled the castle.","53":"I was unable to fulfill a single one of my responsibilities as royalty.","54":"And you, General, kept fulfilling them in my place, all alone!","55":"Lord Leif... Kh... such words... I... I...","56":"I am glad I lived until today... That a day like this... should come again...","57":"Xavier, I apologize as well. I was wrong. Forgive me...","58":"Lord Dorias... \"Forgive me\" is more than I deserve... I only...","59":"Xavier, Lord Leif needs a man like you.","60":"Lend him your strength.","61":"Yes, sir... If an old man like me will do, command me as you will.","62":"To fight the Empire is my dearest wish. Nothing could make me happier!","63":"Prince, the whole castle has been secured. In its fourteenth year, Leonster has at last returned to our hands!","64":"Dorias... thank you.","65":"It is thanks to you that I was able to come this far... I'm grateful.","66":"Lord Leif...","67":"Finn... we've finally come home. Returning together with you was my dream...","68":"...Thank you. I'm truly grateful...","69":"Lord Leif...","70":"Prince! Forgive me for interrupting, but what became of your promise!","71":"Princess Miranda? If it's the liberation of Ulster, I haven't forgotten.","72":"Then please march out right now. If you dawdle, it will be too late!","73":"What do you mean? Has something happened in Ulster?","74":"The citizens are plotting a revolt. But they can't win on their own. At this rate there will be many victims.","75":"Prince Leif, help them! Please help Ulster!!","76":"Prince, forgive me for interrupting, but someone has come wishing an audience.","77":"I am told she has come from Ulster... ah, hey, wait! We do not yet have the prince's permission...","78":"You are Prince Leif!","79":"Please, I beg of you. Ulster... please save Ulster.","80":"Ulster? What do you mean? Would you explain in detail?","81":"I believe you know that our Ulster swore obedience to the Empire, and was thereby allowed to continue.","82":"But the tyranny only grew worse by the day,","83":"and the citizens, unable to bear it, rose in revolt yesterday.","84":"A revolt... But civilians alone can't manage it. Did the Ulster army join them?","85":"No...","86":"We asked the army's commander, Count Conomor, many times,","87":"but he only told us to wait and would not give his leave.","88":"In the end, we rose up without his leave.","89":"But the revolt failed, the imperial army struck back, and many were killed.","90":"Lord Leif, please, please save the people of Ulster! I beg you!!","91":"Understood. Then let's head for Ulster right now.","92":"Lord Leif, you must not!","93":"I understand how you feel, but we do not have the strength now to save Ulster.","94":"Now is the time to defend this Leonster and build up our forces!","95":"I am of the same mind as Lord Dorias.","96":"We must not underestimate the Empire. If we fight them head-on, we have no chance of victory.","97":"Prince, you must not grow proud! Our victories so far were, so to speak, due to the Empire's blunders.","98":"Do not forget that!","99":"Then are you both, Dorias and August, telling me to leave the people of Ulster to die!","100":"When I was small I was sheltered in Ulster, and kept alive by the love of Queen Ethnia.","101":"My father would never forgive forgetting that debt!","102":"If you absolutely will not consent, I will go even by myself. You wait in this castle!","103":"Well, this is a problem... I had thought he had grown up a little more, but Lord Leif seems still very much a child...","104":"...Understood. Then let us go to the relief of Ulster.","105":"First, I will set out ahead, taking half the soldiers.","106":"Prince, you depart tomorrow morning with the remaining soldiers. August, that is acceptable?","107":"Hmm...... So that is how it is......","108":"In that case, I would have you order me to go ahead.","109":"The prince needs you. Stay by his side. There were times we differed, but without you we would not be where we are.","110":"...Continue to be Lord Leif's strength from here on.","111":"...... If you insist so far, there is no help for it.","112":"Dorias, why not the whole army? If you're going ahead, I'll go with you.","113":"Prince! Enough of your willfulness! The soldiers are utterly exhausted.","114":"The veterans especially, with the taking of Leonster as their only support, have pushed themselves beyond all limits.","115":"There, look. Even now they are all sleeping like the dead.","116":"But if you ride out, Prince, they will follow even if they must force themselves.","117":"Is it all right with you to make them push themselves like that?","118":"...I'm sorry. It's as you say, Dorias... I was wrong. But will that be enough fighting strength?","119":"...With the liberation of Leonster, those who had been in hiding","120":"and those who had been working under the Empire against their will have joined us in numbers.","121":"I will take them along to make up the shortfall.","122":"I see. Then I will set out too as soon as preparations are done.","123":"Dorias, I leave the people of Ulster to you. Protect them!","124":"Yes.","125":"But Lord Leif, before I ride out, let me tell you one important thing.","126":"An important thing? What is it, Dorias, so formal all of a sudden?","127":"Leonster has been liberated, and our kingdom has been restored.","128":"With this, Lord Leif, you are formally the heir to the throne of Leonster.","129":"That is to say, you have become \"Prince.\"","130":"Please become a fine sovereign who does not shame that name.","131":"Oh, is that all. I know. I'll become stronger, you'll see.","132":"Until I get Eyvel back, my fight isn't over.","133":"You'll come to Munster with me too, won't you, Dorias?","134":"Sir... Now then, Lord Leif, I ride out.","135":"May God's protection be with you, Lord Leif!","136":"There are some who request an audience with the prince...","137":"It seems they were being forced to work in this castle and were saved by us, or so they say...","138":"Good, I'll see them. Bring them here.","139":"Prince Leif, congratulations on retaking Leonster.","140":"We, too, were saved thanks to you, Prince.","141":"This is just a small token of our thanks. Please accept it.","142":"...I will be your opponent...","143":"Forgive me... Lord Leif... Glory to our Leonster!!","144":"I cannot bear to live in shame any longer... This is the end...","145":"Curse you! I won't lose to the likes of you! I won't lose!","146":"Guh... To the likes of them... I was careless..."};
